Usage: lsof [options]

List open files for running processes on Windows.
This command enumerates kernel handles and prints entries that map to files.
Some handles may require elevated privileges and some object queries can timeout.

OPTIONS:
  -p, --pid NUM              list files opened by process id
  -a, --all                  include non-file handles and unnamed entries
  -d, --descriptor NUM       filter by file descriptor number
  -i, --internet[=ARG]       show internet connections; optional spec ':PORT',
                             'PROTO', 'PROTO:PORT'
  -F, --field                machine-readable field output
  -n, --numeric              do not convert native paths to DOS paths
      --no-headers           print no header line
  -P, --no-port-translation  do not translate port numbers
  -t, --timeout-ms NUM       NtQueryObject timeout in milliseconds
  -u, --user ARG             filter by user (UID or name)
      --help                 display this help and exit
  -V, --version              output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
